<div class="table-100" style="padding: 100px 0;">
  <div class="table-cell-left-50">
    <div class="img-left-wrapper-josh josh-8">
	  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0664/2387/files/adsum-josh-matthews-gary-klein.jpg?4712108941173620911" class="img-right">
      <div class="blog-img-caption" style="text-align: left;">
        Gary Klein, the founder of Klein Bikes.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="table-cell-right-50">
    <div class="josh-text-wrapper">
     <p style="font-weight: 600;">
      Same here. Some of us have our beds on the floor.
     </p>
     <p>
      Haha, I got the closest I could with the bed because I have to store stuff under my bed. I don’t like having a lot of shit but New York makes it look like you have a lot, even if you don’t. 
      <br/><br/>
      Except bikes; I like to have a lot of bikes. I just picked up two more Kleins that will be here next week. I’ve always liked Kleins. The dude, Gary Klein, he was just a wild dude but you see him and it’s like “That’s him!? That’s the fuckin’ guy?” 
      <br/><br/> 
       All the stuff he was doing is insane. He’s an MIT graduate. He was blowing minds engineering wise. To top it off he took that mentality to the paint. That’s why the paint is always so wild. You think he would be like <a href="http://si6.mtb-news.de/fotos/data/500/1010bradbury.jpg" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: underline;">Doug Bradbury</a> from Manitou Cycles. He looked the part. Super handsome. You’re like “Yea, that’s a wild boy.” 
      <br/><br/> 
      Gary Klein was like, “What the fuck?” He looks like a schlub. Can’t judge a book by it’s cover.      
     </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="josh-9" style="margin: 100px auto; max-width: 900px;">
  <img style="display: block; margin: 0 auto; width: 100%;" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0664/2387/files/adsum-josh-matthews_MG_8198.jpg?11585016459499826675">
